{title: There Is a Balm in Gilead}
{artist: Traditional spiritual}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Spiritual}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]There is a balm in Gilead to [C]make the wounded [G]whole
There is a balm in Gilead to [D]heal the sin-sick [G]soul
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Sometimes I feel discouraged and [C]think my work's in [G]vain
But then the Holy Spirit re[D]vives my soul a[G]gain
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]If you cannot preach like Peter, if you [C]cannot pray like [G]Paul
You can tell the love of Jesus and [D]say He died for [G]all
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
